[{"text":"HypExplicit[exp, nu] expresses Hypergeometric functions in exp by their definition in terms of a sum (the Sum is omitted and nu is the summation index).","anchor":"hypexplicit"},{"text":"Overview, HypergeometricIR.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"Hypergeometric2F1[a, b, c, z] HypExplicit[%, \\[Nu]]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\, _2F_1(a,b;c;z)\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{\\Gamma (c) z^{\\nu } \\Gamma (a+\\nu ) \\Gamma (b+\\nu )}{\\Gamma (a) \\Gamma (b) \\Gamma (\\nu +1) \\Gamma (c+\\nu )}\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"HypergeometricPFQ[{a, b, c}, {d, e}, z] HypExplicit[%, \\[Nu]]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\, _3F_2(a,b,c;d,e;z)\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{\\Gamma (d) \\Gamma (e) z^{\\nu } \\Gamma (a+\\nu ) \\Gamma (b+\\nu ) \\Gamma (c+\\nu )}{\\Gamma (a) \\Gamma (b) \\Gamma (c) \\Gamma (\\nu +1) \\Gamma (d+\\nu ) \\Gamma (e+\\nu )}\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"}]